0001: spec:
0002:   grid: 20-27 rows x 22-26 cols
0003:   background: BLACK
0004:   wall_network:
0005:     description: connected rectilinear graph of BLUE wall segments and colored marker nodes partitioning the grid into open regions
0006:     segments: 8-18 straight (H or V) BLUE segments, length 2-11 cells, roughly equal H/V count [observed]
0007:     markers: 9-17 non-blue non-black single cells at every graph node (junction or leaf); each endpoint of a wall segment is a marker or grid boundary
0008:     marker_colors: 3-4 distinct colors (from RED GREEN AZURE YELLOW MAGENTA); each color has 1-6 markers
0009:     connectivity: walls + markers form one 4-connected component; every marker is 4-adjacent to at least one wall cell
0010:   regions:
0011:     count: 6-11 open (BLACK + dot) regions separated by the barrier network
0012:     each region has >=2 adjacent marker colors (8-connected), with exactly one strict majority color
0013:   dots:
0014:     count: 20-35 isolated single BLUE cells (no BLUE 4-neighbor), scattered in passable regions
0015:     every region contains 2-5 dots; min Manhattan distance between dots >=2
0016:   transform: recolor each isolated BLUE dot to the unique majority marker color bordering its region; walls and markers unchanged
0017: 
0018: generation_strategy:
0019:   approach: construct wall graph first, then place markers ensuring majority constraint, then scatter dots
0020:   steps:
0021:     1. Pick grid size in range. Design a rectilinear planar graph on the grid -- place 8-17 node positions at intersections/edges, connect adjacent nodes with H/V blue wall segments of length 2-11.  Ensure walls+markers form one connected component and partition grid into 6-11 regions.
0022:     2. Choose 3-4 marker colors. Assign a color to each node such that every region has a unique strict majority among its bordering nodes. Greedy or constraint propagation works since regions share nodes.
0023:     3. For each region, scatter 2-5 isolated BLUE dots on BLACK cells with no BLUE 4-neighbor (min Manhattan distance 2 between dots).
0024:     4. Output is derived by running the solver (flood-fill regions, count marker votes, recolor dots).
